# Sheltering Ancient "Cumulative upkeep--Put a +1/+1 counter on a creature an opponent controls." (CR 702.24a). At Bot1's turn 3
# upkeep the Ancient gets its first age counter and Bot1 puts a counter on Bot2's Balduvian Bears (the positive control). Bot1 then
# casts Solemnity ("Counters can't be put on creatures", CR 122.6). At turn 5 no age counter is put on the Ancient (it keeps
# its one) and a cost that puts counters on a creature can't be paid (CR 118.3, Solemnity's ruling), the Bears being a creature
# they can't be put on: paying is not offered, the Ancient is sacrificed, and the Bears still has one counter.

